          <p>GOAT delivers the optimal margin-velocity combination: $82.42 avg margin at 7.6-day avg turnover. StockX matches velocity (7.5 days) but costs $8.50/unit in margin. For high-volume operators, that delta compounds to thousands per month. Walk-in Retail's $89.55 margin is the highest, but its 33.3-day avg hold makes it capital-inefficient for active operations — reserve it for high-demand Deadstock units where patience is tolerable.</p>
